<h2><a name=book></hr>Book</a></h2>

<span style='mso-bookmark:book'></span>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><span style='font-size:13.5pt'><a
href="http://www.stat.colostate.edu/computationalstatistics/"><b><span
style='mso-bidi-font-style:italic'>Computational Statistics</span></b></a> by
Geof H. Givens and Jennifer A. Hoeting<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><span style='font-size:13.5pt'>Wiley,
2005<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><span style='mso-bidi-font-weight:
bold'>A comprehensive text on modern and classical methods of statistical
computing and computational statistics with detailed examples and problems drawn
from diverse fields including bioinformatics, ecology, medicine, computer
vision, and stochastic finance.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>R
code available on book website.</span></p>

